  "body": "What happens: main is red after PR #1744 (merge a39e9a8b). The batch gate on m3 (macOS), at a39e9a8b, fails one kernel test:\n\n- `crates/kernel/tests/step_agreement.rs` :: `step_files_agree_or_refuse_by_name` (step_agreement.rs:435)\n\nThe test keeps a list of every STEP file under `testdata/models/`. PR #1744 added two STEP fixtures, `modular_clamp_unit.step` and `modular_lathe_head.step`, but did not add them to the list. The assert gets the two extra names: `left` has 16 files, `right` has 14.\n\nCause: the PR's quick gate did not run the kernel suites, because the kernel crate itself was not changed. The fixture folder is shared test data.\n\nFix: add the two files to the list in step_agreement.rs, with the verdict each one gets (agree, or refuse by name), the same as the other fixtures. Run `cargo test -p camcraft-kernel --release --test step_agreement` (kernel runs in release).\n\nDone means: step_agreement passes on main with the two new fixtures listed and judged. Optional: the quick gate maps `testdata/models/*.step` to the kernel step_agreement suite, so a new fixture runs it.\n",
